Consider this constructor:

public class Dog {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public Dog(String name, int age) {
        name = name;
        age = age;
    }
}

If a Dog is constructed with new Dog("Rex", 3), what will the name and age fields of that Dog object be after construction?

public class Point {
    private int x;
    private int y;

    public Point(int x, int y) {
        this.x = x;
        this.y = y;
    }

    public void shiftX(int x) {
        this.x = this.x + x;
    }
}

A Point object p is created with new Point(5, 10), then p.shiftX(3) is called. What is the value of p's x field afterward?
